From: RelicOS <relicos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: odroid_go2: export the board-id ADC value

oga_read_board_id() returns the *index* into the model table; the raw
SARADC reading it was derived from dies on the stack. The boot script
needs that raw number: RelicOS maps ADC windows to devicetrees in a
text file on the card (Arch-R's layer-2 scheme), so adding a device is
editing a file, not recompiling U-Boot.

Keep the reading in a static and publish it as "hwid_adc" alongside the
other board variables. The name matches Arch-R's on purpose: it is the
same value a later milestone will hand to the kernel as uboot.hwid_adc=.

env_set_ulong() renders the value in decimal (simple_itoa), so scripts
must compare it with "test" (decimal parsing), not "itest" (hex).
---
diff --git a/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c b/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
index 4351de2..1f96586 100644
--- a/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
+++ b/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
@@ -61,6 +61,9 @@ static const struct oga_model oga_model_details[] = {
 	},
 };
 
+/* Raw SARADC reading, kept so it can be exported to the environment. */
+static u32 oga_board_id_adc;
+
 static int oga_read_board_id(void)
 {
 	u32 adc_info;
@@ -72,6 +75,8 @@ static int oga_read_board_id(void)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	oga_board_id_adc = adc_info;
+
 	/*
 	 * Get the correct device from the table. The ADC value is
 	 * determined by a resistor on ADC channel 0. The manufacturer
@@ -105,6 +110,7 @@ static int oga_detect_device(void)
 	env_set("board", oga_model_details[board_id].board);
 	env_set("board_name", oga_model_details[board_id].board_name);
 	env_set("fdtfile", oga_model_details[board_id].fdtfile);
+	env_set_ulong("hwid_adc", oga_board_id_adc);
 
 	return 0;
 }
